th the offset from UTC and the instant as the writer's zone rules gave them, or floating, on the wall clock of wherever the user is, without zone, offset and instant. Defined in spec/time.md. Its schema never changes.","fields":[{"doc":"The year of the proleptic Gregorian calendar, 1 to 9999.","name":"year","type":"int"},{"doc":"The month, 1 (January) to 12 (December).","name":"month","type":"int"},{"doc":"The day of the month, 1 to the number of days of that month in that year.","name":"day","type":"int"},{"doc":"The hour on the wall clock, 0 to 23.","name":"hour","type":"int"},{"doc":"The minute, 0 to 59.","name":"minute","type":"int"},{"doc":"The second, 0 to 59; a leap second is not written as 60.","name":"second","type":"int"},{"doc":"The millisecond, 0 to 999.","name":"millisecond","type":"int"},{"default":null,"doc":"The name of the time zone in the IANA time zone database, such as Europe/Berlin. Null for a floating time; then offset_seconds and instant_ms are null as well.","name":"zone","type":["null","string"]},{"default":null,"doc":"The offset of the wall clock from UTC, in seconds, -64800 to 64800, as the writer's rules of the zone gave it at the instant, such as 3600 for 01:00 east of UTC. Null for a floating time, and only then.","name":"offset_seconds","type":["null","int"]},{"default":null,"doc":"The instant, in milliseconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z without leap seconds: the wall clock read as if it were UTC, minus offset_seconds. Null for a floating time, and only then.","name":"instant_ms","type":["null","long"]}],"name":"DateTime","namespace":"axt","type":"record"}]},{"axt.emoji":"⏹️","axt.help":"When the link ends.","axt.help_translations":{"de":"Wann die Verknüpfung endet."},"axt.label":"Until","axt.label_translations":{"de":"Bis"},"default":null,"doc":"The first moment after the link, as for the end of an appointment. Null when it has no end or it is not known.","name":"end","type":["null","axt.DateTime"]},{"axt.advanced":true,"axt.emoji":"🗂️